{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery with minimal use of full_rotate. Recovery states are one-shot and return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception; all controllable actions are open-loop pulses.",
    "Specification automaton binds perception outcomes to safe, coverage-oriented motion, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration after obstacles."
